# Every pattern here was checked against `git ls-files`:
#  - untracked / gitignored local state: node_modules, dist, .env*, .runtime, .tmp-*,
#    .npm-cache, graft, python/tmp*, .research-registry and the .lpbf-* data
#    directories listed below
#  - tracked but not needed to build, test or run the app: .git, .github, .claude,
#    .agents, .cursor, .gemini, sonkayıtlar and the stale tracked **/__pycache__ files
#  - local orchestration state (untracked): .orchestra* covers .orchestra/ and .orchestra-run/; logs written
#    there during a build would otherwise change the build context and invalidate the verify cache
#  - untracked local payloads, caches and scratch trees that a developer checkout has but a CI checkout
#    does not, so a local image matches a CI image: virtualenvs, nested .env files, root tmp* and
#    python/.tmp-* test directories, warp/pytest caches, python/python, python/scratch-manufactured,
#    python/codex-lpbf-test-tmp, python/lpbf-run-shape-*, the compiled OpenFOAM tree and the gitignored
#    data/benchmark/**/raw measurement payloads (data/benchmark/nist-amb2022-03/raw alone is about 525 MB)
#  - spparks: a gitlink (optional solver checkout, about 250 MB when populated); CI checks out no submodules
#    and nothing in the build, the tests or the server reads it
# NOT excluded on purpose: docs/sources/in625 (read at run time by the server), *.log (tracked evidence logs under docs/), docs/, data/, scripts/, tests/.
node_modules
dist
.orchestra*
.runtime
.tmp-*
.npm-cache
**/.env
**/.env.*
!.env.example
.venv
**/.venv
/tmp*
python/.tmp-*
**/.warp-cache
**/.pytest_cache
python/python
python/scratch-manufactured
python/codex-lpbf-test-tmp
python/lpbf-run-shape-*
python/openfoam/bin
python/openfoam/Make/linux*
data/benchmark/**/raw
spparks
.git
.github
graft
python/tmp*
.lpbf-jobs
.lpbf-runs
.lpbf-sources
.lpbf-run-bundles
.research-registry
.claude
.agents
.cursor
.gemini
sonkayıtlar
**/__pycache__
